    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm an admin at a law firm and we're looking to move away from SMS-based 2FA because of the interception risks. Can you give me a step-by-step guide on how to implement hardware security keys (like YubiKeys) for our staff instead? Need to know the deployment process and how to handle onboarding for non-technical users.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, procure the necessary hardware security keys and select a suitable authentication system that supports FIDO2/U2F protocols. Next, configure your core applications and systems to accept your organization's generated security keys as a secondary factor. For user onboarding, provide clear, in-person training sessions where staff physically register their keys with IT support. This hands-on approach ensures non-technical users understand the basic login procedure and practice key registration in a guided setting.",
