    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense, hands on is probably best. one thing though—when we're talking about the 'threat actors' or people trying to get into the system, what are the main ways they'll try to bypass these physical keys? like, if we switch to Yubikeys, what are we actually stopping?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
