      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. so if we're mainly stopping remote stuff, what about the 'human element'? like, are there specific social engineering tactics people use to try and trick employees into handing over access or bypassing the hardware requirement? just want to make sure our training covers the right stuff.",
